<!-- Plugin Configuration File. Read more: https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/plugin-configuration-file.html -->
<idea-plugin>
    <!-- Unique identifier of the plugin. It should be FQN. It cannot be changed between the plugin versions. -->
    <id>de.kumpewo.intellij-autohotkey</id>

    <!-- Public plugin name should be written in Title Case.
     Guidelines: https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/marketplace/best-practices-for-listing.html#plugin-name -->
    <name>AutoHotkey v2 Language Support</name>

    <!-- A displayed Vendor name or Organization ID displayed on the Plugins Page. -->
    <vendor url="https://www.kumpewo.de">Kumpewo</vendor>

    <!-- Description of the plugin displayed on the Plugin Page and IDE Plugin Manager.
         Guidelines: https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/marketplace/best-practices-for-listing.html#plugin-description -->
    <description><![CDATA[
<p>Complete support for <a href="https://www.autohotkey.com/">AutoHotkey</a> v2 in IntelliJ IDEA, PyCharm, WebStorm and
the other JetBrains IDEs: a real parser, completion that knows the AutoHotkey help, the original documentation where
you need it, a debugger, and running, validating and compiling scripts without leaving the editor.</p>

<p><b>Everything you expect from a language plugin</b></p>
<ul>
  <li>Syntax and error highlighting from a real parser, with colors by role: flow control, directives, built-in
      variables, functions, classes, methods and properties, hotkeys, hotstrings, labels.</li>
  <li>Code formatter with its own code style page; optionally adjusts the case of keywords and built-in names
      (<code>msgbox</code> becomes <code>MsgBox</code>).</li>
  <li>Structure view, breadcrumbs, sticky lines, code folding (also <code>;region</code>), brace matching,
      highlighting of the occurrences of a name, spell checking of comments and strings.</li>
  <li>Live templates for functions, classes, loops, hotkeys and Gui windows, <i>Surround With</i> and a template
      for new scripts.</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Completion that saves you a trip to the help</b></p>
<p>Besides built-in and own names, members and key names, the plugin completes what usually sends you to the
documentation: the values and options inside strings.</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>MsgBox "Saved", "Title", "|"</code> offers <code>YesNo</code>, <code>Iconi</code>, <code>T&hellip;</code>
      and the other options of a message box.</li>
  <li><code>MyGui.Add("|")</code> offers the control types; <code>MyGui.Add("Edit", "w200 |")</code> the options of
      an Edit control: <code>ReadOnly</code>, <code>Number</code>, <code>Limit&hellip;</code>, <code>WantTab</code>
      &hellip;</li>
  <li><code>btn.OnEvent("|")</code> offers the events of a button (<code>Click</code>, <code>DoubleClick</code>
      &hellip;), <code>CoordMode "|"</code> its modes, <code>Send "{|"</code> and the hotkey before <code>::</code>
      the key names.</li>
  <li><code>#Include &lt;</code> lists the files of your library folders.</li>
</ul>
<p>Parameter info shows the parameters of built-in functions and methods, of your own functions, and the
description of the current parameter from your doc comment.</p>

<p><b>The original help, right where you need it</b></p>
<ul>
  <li><i>Ctrl+Q</i> or hovering shows the page of the AutoHotkey help for the word under the caret, chosen by its
      role: <code>Gui.Add</code> and <code>Menu.Add</code> lead to different pages, a nested class like
      <code>Gui.Button</code> to its own.</li>
  <li><i>Shift+F1</i> opens the topic in <code>AutoHotkey.chm</code> of your installation.</li>
  <li>Help for the plugin's pragmas and for the Ahk2Exe compiler directives; the AutoHotkey help and a complete
      user manual in the <i>Help</i> menu.</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Tell the plugin what your variables are</b></p>
<p>AutoHotkey decides the class of a value only at run time. One comment line closes that gap:
<code>;@declare-type win as Gui</code> lets <code>win.</code> offer exactly the members of <code>Gui</code>, narrows
the parameter info and the help to that class, and works with your own classes as well. <code>;@declare-auto-type</code>
declares whole groups by name, <code>;@declare-private</code> marks private members, and a <code>pragmas.ahk</code>
included by your scripts holds the declarations for a whole project.</p>

<p><b>Document your own code</b></p>
<p>Doc comments <code>/** ... */</code> before functions, methods and classes, with Markdown and the tags
<code>@param</code>, <code>@returns</code>, <code>@throws</code>, <code>@example</code>, <code>@see</code> and
<code>@deprecated</code>, appear in the quick documentation, in the completion list and in the parameter info.
<code>@param {Gui} win</code> declares the type of a parameter, deprecated definitions are struck out where they are
used, <code>/**</code> + <i>Enter</i> writes the skeleton, and the formatter can align and wrap the comments with
settings like those for JavaDoc.</p>

<p><b>Your own library, a year later</b></p>
<p>This is where the pieces come together. You write a library once and document it. Months later you type
<code>#Include &lt;</code> and pick it from the list. A declared variable completes the method names of your class,
<i>Ctrl+Q</i> on a method shows what you wrote about it, and the parameter info reminds you what each argument
means. Your own libraries stay easy to use, even when you are no longer deep in their details.</p>

<p><b>Find your way</b></p>
<p>Wherever you want to go, the plugin takes you there: <i>Ctrl+B</i> to functions, classes, methods, properties,
fields, labels and <code>#Include</code> files (including the AutoHotkey library folders), <i>Find Usages</i>,
<i>Rename</i> with preview, <i>Go to Symbol</i> and <i>Go to Class</i> across the project, and the structure of the
file. Local variables and parameters of functions follow the scoping rules of AutoHotkey and are renamed right in
the editor.</p>

<p><b>Run, validate, debug, compile</b></p>
<ul>
  <li>Run configurations with clickable load errors; the launcher or the matching v2 interpreter is chosen by
      <code>#Requires</code>.</li>
  <li><i>Validate with AutoHotkey</i> checks the script with <code>/validate</code> (manually, on save or after
      reformatting) and marks the error line in the editor; warnings of <code>#Warn</code> appear in the
      console.</li>
  <li>A debugger built on the DBGp engine of AutoHotkey v2: breakpoints (also conditional and logging), stepping,
      call stack, variables and objects, changing values, inline values in the editor, exception breakpoints and
      attaching to a running script.</li>
  <li>Compiling with Ahk2Exe from the <code>;@Ahk2Exe-...</code> directives in the script, and running the
      compiled console program in the IDE.</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Good to know</b></p>
<ul>
  <li>The plugin understands AutoHotkey v2. Files with <code>#Requires AutoHotkey v1</code> are left unparsed; for
      files without <code>#Requires</code> it detects v1 code and offers to insert the right line.</li>
  <li>There is no type inference: navigation and completion work by name (local variables and parameters by
      function), so check the preview of a rename.</li>
  <li>Editing works without AutoHotkey; running, validating, debugging and compiling need an AutoHotkey v2
      installation (Windows).</li>
</ul>

<p>Free and open source (GPL-2.0-or-later).
<a href="https://github.com/Kumpewo/intellij-autohotkey">Source code, issues and feedback on GitHub</a>.</p>
        ]]></description>

    <!-- Product and plugin compatibility requirements.
         Read more: https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/plugin-compatibility.html -->
    <!-- only platform modules: the plugin runs in every IntelliJ-based IDE (IDEA, PyCharm, WebStorm ...) -->
    <depends>com.intellij.modules.platform</depends>
    <depends>com.intellij.modules.xdebugger</depends>
    <!-- spell checking of comments, strings and hotstrings (spellchecker module of the platform) -->
    <depends optional="true" config-file="ahk-spellchecker.xml">com.intellij.modules.spellchecker</depends>


    <!-- Extensions defined by the plugin.
         Read more: https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/plugin-extension-points.html -->
    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij">
        <fileType
                name="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.AhkFileType"
                fieldName="INSTANCE"
                language="AutoHotkey"
                extensions="ahk"/>
        <lang.parserDefinition
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.parser.AhkParserDefinition"/>
        <lang.syntaxHighlighterFactory
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.highlighting.AhkSyntaxHighlighterFactory"/>
        <lang.braceMatcher
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.highlighting.AhkBraceMatcher"/>
        <colorSettingsPage
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.highlighting.AhkColorSettingsPage"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkBlockBraceAnnotator"/>
        <!-- doc comments: unknown @param / classes, deprecated definitions struck out -->
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkDocCommentAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkElseBodyAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkBadCommentAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkIgnoredLineAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkVersionAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkDeclAnnotator"/>
        <!-- mandatory parameter after an optional one: v2.1 only -->
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkParameterOrderAnnotator"/>
        <!-- #Module / #Import: v2.1 only, where allowed, module name -->
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkModuleAnnotator"/>
        <!-- function definition expressions: v2.1 only, not a statement on their own -->
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkFuncExprAnnotator"/>
        <!-- typed properties and union blocks: v2.1 only, only in a class body -->
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkTypedPropertyAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkTypeDeclarationAnnotator"/>
        <!-- No "Non-ASCII characters" warning for names (AutoHotkey allows them, e.g. "§" as prefix) -->
        <lang.inspectionSuppressor language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkInspectionSuppressor"/>
        <highlightErrorFilter
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkIgnoredLineErrorFilter"/>
        <highlightErrorFilter
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkSyntaxErrorFilter"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkSyntaxErrorAnnotator"/>
        <annotator language="AutoHotkey"
                   implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.validate.AhkValidationAnnotator"/>
        <lang.psiStructureViewFactory
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.structure.AhkStructureViewFactory"/>
        <completion.contributor
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.completion.AhkCompletionContributor"/>
        <typedHandler
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.completion.AhkTypedHandler"/>
        <codeInsight.parameterInfo
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.completion.AhkParameterInfoHandler"/>
        <lang.quoteHandler
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.completion.AhkQuoteHandler"/>
        <breadcrumbsInfoProvider
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.structure.AhkBreadcrumbsProvider"/>
        <!-- code folding: braces, block comments, continuation sections, comment and #Include runs, ;region -->
        <lang.foldingBuilder
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.structure.AhkFoldingBuilder"/>
        <!-- highlight the occurrences of the name under the caret (same name, case-insensitive) -->
        <highlightUsagesHandlerFactory
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkHighlightUsagesHandlerFactory"/>
        <!-- Find Usages (Alt+F7): file of the definition and the files that include it directly -->
        <lang.findUsagesProvider
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkFindUsagesProvider"/>
        <referencesSearch
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkReferencesSearcher"/>
        <!-- the name of a field in its definition is a target (Find Usages and Rename there) -->
        <targetElementEvaluator
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkTargetElementEvaluator"/>
        <!-- Go to Symbol / Go to Class: project-wide search over all definitions (index of the names) -->
        <fileBasedIndex
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkSymbolIndex"/>
        <gotoSymbolContributor
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkGotoSymbolContributor"/>
        <gotoClassContributor
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkGotoClassContributor"/>
        <!-- Rename (Shift+F6) with forced preview, also in indirectly including files, comments and strings -->
        <renamePsiElementProcessor
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkRenameProcessor"/>
        <lang.namesValidator
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkNamesValidator"/>
        <lang.refactoringSupport
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkRefactoringSupportProvider"/>
        <!-- Shift+F6 where nothing can be renamed: a hint instead of silence -->
        <renameHandler implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkRenameHintHandler"/>
        <vetoRenameCondition
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkRenameVeto"/>
        <additionalTextAttributes scheme="Default" file="colorSchemes/AhkDefault.xml"/>
        <additionalTextAttributes scheme="Darcula" file="colorSchemes/AhkDarcula.xml"/>
        <additionalLibraryRootsProvider
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.include.AhkLibraryRootsProvider"/>
        <lang.formatter
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.formatter.AhkFormattingModelBuilder"/>
        <!-- Adjusts the case when formatting (main switch in the code style settings) -->
        <postFormatProcessor
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.formatter.AhkCasePostFormatProcessor"/>
        <!-- doc comments: the lines with * get the indentation of the /** line -->
        <postFormatProcessor
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.formatter.AhkDocCommentPostFormatProcessor"/>
        <codeStyleSettingsProvider
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.formatter.AhkCodeStyleSettingsProvider"/>
        <langCodeStyleSettingsProvider
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.formatter.AhkLanguageCodeStyleSettingsProvider"/>
<!--        <psi.referenceContributor-->
<!--                language="AutoHotkey"-->
<!--                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkReferenceContributor"/>-->
        <psi.referenceContributor
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkLabelReferenceContributor"/>
        <psi.referenceContributor
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.navigation.AhkDefinitionReferenceContributor"/>
        <psi.referenceContributor
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.include.AhkIncludeReferenceContributor"/>
        <psi.referenceContributor
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.module.AhkModuleReferenceContributor"/>
        <lang.commenter
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.formatter.AhkCommenter"/>
        <!-- doc comments: skeleton after /** + Enter, " * " on new lines -->
        <enterHandlerDelegate
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.template.AhkDocEnterHandler"/>
        <lang.documentationProvider
                language="AutoHotkey"
                implementationClass="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.documentation.AhkDocumentationProvider"/>
        <applicationConfigurable
                parentId="language"
                id="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.settings"
                displayName="AutoHotkey"
                instance="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.settings.AhkSettingsConfigurable"/>
        <configurationType
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.run.AhkRunConfigurationType"/>
        <runConfigurationProducer
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.run.AhkRunConfigurationProducer"/>
        <!-- Debugger (DBGp, debug/) -->
        <programRunner implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.debug.AhkDebugRunner"/>
        <xdebugger.breakpointType implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.debug.AhkLineBreakpointType"/>
        <xdebugger.breakpointType implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.debug.AhkExceptionBreakpointType"/>
        <!-- Live templates and file template -->
        <defaultLiveTemplates file="/liveTemplates/AutoHotkey.xml"/>
        <liveTemplateContext
                contextId="AUTOHOTKEY"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.template.AhkTemplateContextType$Generic"/>
        <liveTemplateContext
                contextId="AUTOHOTKEY_CODE"
                baseContextId="AUTOHOTKEY"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.template.AhkTemplateContextType$Code"/>
        <liveTemplateContext
                contextId="AUTOHOTKEY_COMMENT"
                baseContextId="AUTOHOTKEY"
                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.template.AhkTemplateContextType$Comment"/>
        <internalFileTemplate name="AutoHotkey Script"/>
        <!-- Alt+Enter: insert a head of Ahk2Exe compiler directives (compile/AhkAhk2ExeHeader) -->
        <intentionAction>
            <language>AutoHotkey</language>
            <className>de.kumpewo.autohotkey.compile.AhkAddAhk2ExeHeaderIntention</className>
            <bundleName>messages.AhkBundle</bundleName>
            <categoryKey>intention.category</categoryKey>
        </intentionAction>
        <!-- Language level of the current file in the status bar and after AutoHotkey files in the Project view (level/) -->
        <statusBarWidgetFactory id="AutoHotkey.LanguageLevel"
                                implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.level.AhkLevelWidgetFactory"/>
        <projectViewNodeDecorator implementation="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.level.AhkLevelDecorator"/>
        <!-- Alt+Enter anywhere: insert #Requires (annotation/AhkAddRequiresIntention; v1 variant only for v1 code) -->
        <intentionAction>
            <language>AutoHotkey</language>
            <className>de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkAddRequiresIntention</className>
            <bundleName>messages.AhkBundle</bundleName>
            <categoryKey>intention.category</categoryKey>
        </intentionAction>
        <intentionAction>
            <language>AutoHotkey</language>
            <className>de.kumpewo.autohotkey.annotation.AhkAddRequiresIntention$V1</className>
            <descriptionDirectoryName>AhkAddRequiresIntentionV1</descriptionDirectoryName>
            <bundleName>messages.AhkBundle</bundleName>
            <categoryKey>intention.category</categoryKey>
        </intentionAction>
        <!-- Balloon notifications (e.g. "Compile with Ahk2Exe" without ;@Ahk2Exe-Base) -->
        <notificationGroup id="AutoHotkey" displayType="BALLOON" bundle="messages.AhkBundle" key="notification.group"/>
    </extensions>

    <!-- Texts of the actions: action.<id>.text / .description -->
    <resource-bundle>messages.AhkBundle</resource-bundle>
    <actions>
        <action id="AutoHotkey.NewFile" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.template.AhkCreateFileAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="NewGroup" anchor="after" relative-to-action="NewFile"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Validation with AutoHotkey /validate (AhkValidator) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.Validate" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.validate.AhkValidateAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <keyboard-shortcut keymap="$default" first-keystroke="alt shift V"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="CodeMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="ProjectViewPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Compilation into an executable with Ahk2Exe (AhkCompiler) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.Compile" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.compile.AhkCompileAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="CodeMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="ProjectViewPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Copying a tool to its local target as described by settings.ahk-plugin.ini (install/AhkInstaller) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.Install" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.install.AhkInstallAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="CodeMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="ProjectViewPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Documented default settings.ahk-plugin.ini (install/AhkSettingsFile) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.CreateSettings" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.install.AhkCreateSettingsAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="CodeMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="ProjectViewPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Version line ;@Ahk2Exe-SetVersion, commit and tag (install/AhkSetVersion) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.SetVersion" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.install.AhkSetVersionAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="CodeMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="EditorPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
            <add-to-group group-id="ProjectViewPopupMenu" anchor="last"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Attach the debugger to a running script (AhkAttach) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.AttachDebugger" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.debug.AhkAttachAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="RunMenu" anchor="after" relative-to-action="XDebugger.AttachToProcess"/>
        </action>
        <!-- User manual of the plugin (help/extra/, AhkManual) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.Manual" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.documentation.AhkManualAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="HelpMenu" anchor="after" relative-to-action="HelpTopics"/>
        </action>
        <!-- Help of AutoHotkey v2.0 and v2.1 (AhkExternalHelp.openDocs) -->
        <action id="AutoHotkey.Help" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.documentation.AhkHelpAction" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="HelpMenu" anchor="after" relative-to-action="AutoHotkey.Manual"/>
        </action>
        <action id="AutoHotkey.HelpV21" class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.documentation.AhkHelpAction$V21" icon="/icons/autohotkey.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="HelpMenu" anchor="after" relative-to-action="AutoHotkey.Help"/>
        </action>
    </actions>

    <!-- Automatic validation after saving / after Reformat Code (setting "Validate with AutoHotkey") -->
    <applicationListeners>
        <listener class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.validate.AhkValidateTriggers"
                  topic="com.intellij.openapi.fileEditor.FileDocumentManagerListener"/>
        <listener class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.validate.AhkValidateTriggers"
                  topic="com.intellij.openapi.actionSystem.ex.AnActionListener"/>
        <!-- New empty .ahk file created by the IDE ("New > File"): content of the file template (AhkNewFileListener) -->
        <listener class="de.kumpewo.autohotkey.template.AhkNewFileListener"
                  topic="com.intellij.openapi.vfs.newvfs.BulkFileListener"/>
    </applicationListeners>
</idea-plugin>
